wlcore: sdio: honour the clock-xtal DT property

6.6 only parses clock-xtal in wlcore/spi.c; the WL1271 on the Nest J49 is on SDIO
with a 26 MHz crystal (WL12XX_REFCLOCK_26_XTAL in the stock board file). Without
it the firmware boots but never raises its IRQ (ELP wakeup timeout, 0 scan results).

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: J49 project <j49@users.noreply.github.com>

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ti/wlcore/sdio.c	2026-10-28 22:12:24.372403240 +0100
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ti/wlcore/sdio.c	2026-10-28 22:12:23.914739915 +0100
@@ -240,6 +240,8 @@
 	/* optional clock frequency params */
 	of_property_read_u32(np, "ref-clock-frequency",
 			     &pdev_data->ref_clock_freq);
+	/* like wlcore/spi.c: WL127x boards with a crystal reference (e.g. Nest j49) */
+	pdev_data->ref_clock_xtal = of_property_read_bool(np, "clock-xtal");
 	of_property_read_u32(np, "tcxo-clock-frequency",
 			     &pdev_data->tcxo_clock_freq);
 
